  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV and AIDS prevention project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For nine years 2003-12 CAFOD has worked with Caritas Bangladesh to help establish protective measures against the spread of the HIV virus.  To begin with a Trainer Team was set up within Caritas to carry out regional and field level training among Caritas staff and other key personnel.  Suitable educational material was selected and translated into Bangla as a resource for people needing both to obtain factual data, and to explore the ethical and theological issues.  Through a pilot project in Satkhira Sub-District, Khulna District, a successful model was developed for disseminating HIV-awareness quickly and effectively to large numbers of adolescents through the training of peer educators &#x2013; young volunteers who will then pass on what they learn to their friends, and also be ready to provide support.  Caritas is presently replicating this model and rolling it out to Dhaka and Chittagong.  Spiritual counselling is also provided to people living with HIV/ AIDS, and for their families.   Thankfully the HIV prevalence rate in the country has remained consistently very low.</narrative>
  </description>
